  sd(Ahat) under the isotropic null (primary config) = 3.30; analytic = 2.98
  -> an E[Ahat]=+1 AQUAL signal registers at ~0.30 sigma; AQUAL-vs-BranchB separation (1-0.304) at ~0.21 sigma.
  THE KILL CONDITIONS CANNOT TRIGGER HERE: the pre-registered 3-sigma AQUAL-vs-BranchB test needs N~1157 (canonical) / N~1424 (alt) usable galaxies; this firing has n=25. No verdict on AQUAL vs Branch B vs pure MI is possible at this N; the value of this run is the pipeline at scale + the number on record.
  [x-clamp flags, primary config] 8/25 below the banked map range (clamped UP to x=0.05; every clamped galaxy has r=x/e > 1, above the banked reversal crossing at r=0.72-0.97, so no sign-reversal risk), 1/25 above (clamped down to x=0.5).

